# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Recap of the spinless 1D Fermi-Hubbard system {#1-recap-of-the-spinless-1d-fermi-hubbard-system}"
msgstr "1. Recap ng spinless 1D Fermi-Hubbard system {#1-recap-of-the-spinless-1d-fermi-hubbard-system}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The 1D guide writes the model with **vertex** and **transfer** operators,\n"
"$V_j = 1 - 2a_j^\\dagger a_j$ and $T_{jk} = -\\tfrac12 (a_j^\\dagger - a_j)(a_k^\\dagger + a_k)$. With these operators,\n"
"hopping is $t\\,(T_{j,j+1} + T_{j+1,j})$, and the density-density interaction is a product of $V$ operators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isinusulat ng 1D guide ang model gamit ang mga **vertex** at **transfer** operator,\n"
"$V_j = 1 - 2a_j^\\dagger a_j$ at $T_{jk} = -\\tfrac12 (a_j^\\dagger - a_j)(a_k^\\dagger + a_k)$. Gamit ang mga operator na ito,\n"
"ang hopping ay $t\\,(T_{j,j+1} + T_{j+1,j})$, at ang density-density interaction ay produkto ng mga $V$ operator.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/0b9ab5a2-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/0b9ab5a2-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial reuses three main ideas from that guide:\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit muli ang tutorial na ito ng tatlong pangunahing ideya mula sa guide na iyon:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Group terms before you map them.** Transfer operators along a directed path commute, and form a *flow set*. On a chain, the flow sets are the\n"
"east-pointing arrows (dark orange), the west-pointing arrows (light orange), and the diagonal interaction terms. The\n"
"drawing shows the arrows of the spinless chain between its sites. Spinless sites are blue in every drawing.\n"
msgstr ""
"**I-group ang mga term bago i-map.** Nagko-commute ang mga transfer operator sa isang directed path, at bumubuo ng *flow set*. Sa isang chain, ang mga flow set ay ang\n"
"mga arrow na nakaturo sa silangan (madilim na orange), ang mga arrow na nakaturo sa kanluran (matingkad na orange), at ang mga diagonal na interaction term. Ipinapakita ng\n"
"drawing ang mga arrow ng spinless chain sa pagitan ng mga site nito. Asul ang mga spinless site sa bawat drawing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Use an ancilla qubit to gain structure.** The parity-delocalized fermion-to-qubit encoding stores cumulative parities.\n"
"One extra qubit (an ancilla, which is green in every drawing) turns a whole flow set into weight-1 Pauli operators.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Gumamit ng ancilla qubit para magkaroon ng istruktura.** Iniimbak ng parity-delocalized fermion-to-qubit encoding ang mga cumulative parity.\n"
"Ang isang dagdag na qubit (isang ancilla, na berde sa bawat drawing) ay ginagawang weight-1 Pauli operator ang buong flow set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Use the structure to synthesize circuits.** A single Clifford circuit diagonalizes a whole flow set, so the circuit depth does not\n"
"grow with the chain length.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Gamitin ang istruktura para mag-synthesize ng mga circuit.** Ang isang Clifford circuit ay nagdi-diagonalize ng buong flow set, kaya hindi lumalaki ang circuit depth\n"
"kasabay ng haba ng chain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Spin: blocked or interleaved mode ordering {#2-spin-blocked-or-interleaved-mode-ordering}"
msgstr "2. Spin: blocked o interleaved na mode ordering {#2-spin-blocked-or-interleaved-mode-ordering}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses the spinful Fermi-Hubbard model. On a 1D chain of sites, its Hamiltonian is as follows:\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng tutorial na ito ang spinful Fermi-Hubbard model. Sa isang 1D chain ng mga site, ang Hamiltonian nito ay ang sumusunod:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{j,\\sigma} \\left(a_{j\\sigma}^\\dagger a_{j+1,\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.}\\right) +\n"
"\\frac{U}{2} \\sum_j \\left(n_{j\\uparrow} - \\tfrac12\\right)\\left(n_{j\\downarrow} - \\tfrac12\\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H = -t \\sum_{j,\\sigma} \\left(a_{j\\sigma}^\\dagger a_{j+1,\\sigma} + \\text{h.c.}\\right) +\n"
"\\frac{U}{2} \\sum_j \\left(n_{j\\uparrow} - \\tfrac12\\right)\\left(n_{j\\downarrow} - \\tfrac12\\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The vertex and transfer operators do not represent spin. They see $2L$ fermionic modes, so you decide which mode index\n"
"belongs to which (site, spin) pair. Two orderings are natural: **blocked** (all spin-up modes first, then all spin-down\n"
"modes) and **interleaved** (the spin-up and spin-down modes of a site next to each other). Both orderings describe the same physics, but they\n"
"couple different modes, and the encoding and the hardware see those couplings.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi kinakatawan ng mga vertex at transfer operator ang spin. Nakikita nila ang $2L$ fermionic mode, kaya ikaw ang magpapasya kung aling mode index\n"
"ang para sa aling (site, spin) na pares. Dalawang ordering ang natural: **blocked** (lahat ng spin-up mode muna, saka lahat ng spin-down\n"
"mode) at **interleaved** (ang spin-up at spin-down mode ng isang site ay magkatabi). Parehong inilalarawan ng dalawang ordering ang parehong physics, ngunit\n"
"nagko-couple sila ng magkakaibang mode, at nakikita ng encoding at ng hardware ang mga coupling na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The choice of ordering changes the distance that the hopping terms and the on-site interaction terms must cover:\n"
msgstr "Binabago ng pagpili ng ordering ang distansyang dapat sakupin ng mga hopping term at ng mga on-site interaction term:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Ordering | Spin-up site $j$ | Spin-down site $j$ | Modes that a hop connects | Modes that the on-site term connects |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| **Blocked** | $j$ | $L + j$ | $j \\leftrightarrow j+1$ | $j \\leftrightarrow L + j$ |\n"
"| **Interleaved** | $2j$ | $2j + 1$ | $2j \\leftrightarrow 2j+2$ | $2j \\leftrightarrow 2j+1$ |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Ordering | Spin-up site $j$ | Spin-down site $j$ | Mga mode na ikinokonekta ng isang hop | Mga mode na ikinokonekta ng on-site term |\n"
"|---|---|---|---|---|\n"
"| **Blocked** | $j$ | $L + j$ | $j \\leftrightarrow j+1$ | $j \\leftrightarrow L + j$ |\n"
"| **Interleaved** | $2j$ | $2j + 1$ | $2j \\leftrightarrow 2j+2$ | $2j \\leftrightarrow 2j+1$ |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following drawing shows both orderings for $L = 4$ sites. Each node is a mode ($V_m$, as in section 1) at the horizontal\n"
"position of its mode index. The spin-up modes are on the top chain (dark blue), and the spin-down modes are on the bottom chain\n"
"(light blue). The arrows along a chain are the hops. East-pointing hops are dark orange and west-pointing hops are light orange, as in\n"
"the flow sets of section 1. The dotted blue link between the two modes of a site is the on-site interaction, and the grid\n"
"marks the position of every mode on the line.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na drawing ang parehong ordering para sa $L = 4$ na site. Ang bawat node ay isang mode ($V_m$, tulad ng sa section 1) sa horizontal\n"
"na posisyon ng mode index nito. Ang mga spin-up mode ay nasa itaas na chain (madilim na asul), at ang mga spin-down mode ay nasa ibabang chain\n"
"(matingkad na asul). Ang mga arrow sa isang chain ay ang mga hop. Madilim na orange ang mga hop na nakaturo sa silangan at matingkad na orange ang mga nakaturo sa kanluran, tulad ng sa\n"
"mga flow set ng section 1. Ang tuldok-tuldok na asul na link sa pagitan ng dalawang mode ng isang site ay ang on-site interaction, at minamarkahan ng grid\n"
"ang posisyon ng bawat mode sa linya.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c353bde8-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c353bde8-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The ordering is visible in the on-site links. In blocked order, the on-site links are long, because the on-site term couples mode $j$ and\n"
"mode $L + j$, while the hops stay between neighboring modes. In interleaved order, the on-site links are short (mode $2j$ to mode\n"
"$2j + 1$), but the hops skip over the mode of the other spin. In both orderings, every term still acts on **two modes**.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita ang ordering sa mga on-site link. Sa blocked order, mahaba ang mga on-site link, dahil ina-couple ng on-site term ang mode $j$ at\n"
"mode $L + j$, habang nananatili ang mga hop sa pagitan ng magkakatabing mode. Sa interleaved order, maikli ang mga on-site link (mode $2j$ hanggang mode\n"
"$2j + 1$), ngunit lumalaktaw ang mga hop sa mode ng kabilang spin. Sa parehong ordering, bawat term ay kumikilos pa rin sa **dalawang mode**.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $m(j, \\sigma)$ is the mode of site $j$ and spin $\\sigma$, hopping becomes\n"
"$t\\,(T_{m(j,\\sigma),\\,m(j+1,\\sigma)} + T_{m(j+1,\\sigma),\\,m(j,\\sigma)})$ between neighbors with the same spin, and the on-site term is\n"
"$\\tfrac{U}{8} V_{m(j,\\uparrow)} V_{m(j,\\downarrow)}$. The following code builds these terms and prints them, one flow set\n"
"at a time, for $L = 2$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung ang $m(j, \\sigma)$ ang mode ng site $j$ at spin $\\sigma$, ang hopping ay nagiging\n"
"$t\\,(T_{m(j,\\sigma),\\,m(j+1,\\sigma)} + T_{m(j+1,\\sigma),\\,m(j,\\sigma)})$ sa pagitan ng magkakatabing may parehong spin, at ang on-site term ay\n"
"$\\tfrac{U}{8} V_{m(j,\\uparrow)} V_{m(j,\\downarrow)}$. Binubuo ng sumusunod na code ang mga term na ito at piniprint ang mga ito, isang flow set\n"
"sa bawat pagkakataon, para sa $L = 2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**At the fermionic level, the choice of ordering is only a naming convention.** Blocked and interleaved order give each fermionic mode\n"
"a different index, and nothing else changes. The Hamiltonian is the same operator, with its modes renamed. You can verify this\n"
"with `relabel_modes`, which renames mode $i$ to `permutation[i]` in every term of a `TransferVertexOperator`.\n"
"Anticommutation has no effect, because the operation renames the labels of the modes and does not move particles past each other.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Sa fermionic na antas, pangalan lamang ang pagpili ng ordering.** Binibigyan ng blocked at interleaved order ang bawat fermionic mode\n"
"ng ibang index, at walang ibang nagbabago. Ang Hamiltonian ay ang parehong operator, na may pinalitan na pangalan ang mga mode nito. Maaari mo itong i-verify\n"
"gamit ang `relabel_modes`, na nagpapalit ng pangalan ng mode $i$ tungo sa `permutation[i]` sa bawat term ng isang `TransferVertexOperator`.\n"
"Walang epekto ang anticommutation, dahil pinapalitan lang ng operasyon ang mga label ng mga mode at hindi nito inililipat ang mga particle sa isa't isa.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider the permutation that takes each blocked index to the interleaved index of the same (site, spin) pair. If this permutation,\n"
"applied to the blocked Hamiltonian, gives the interleaved Hamiltonian, then the two orderings are the same model, and they have the same spectrum\n"
"and Trotter error. A difference can appear only *after* an encoding, where the index decides which qubits are neighbors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isaalang-alang ang permutation na nagmamapa sa bawat blocked index tungo sa interleaved index ng parehong (site, spin) na pares. Kung ang permutation na ito,\n"
"kapag inilapat sa blocked Hamiltonian, ay nagbibigay ng interleaved Hamiltonian, ang dalawang ordering ay iisang model, at pareho ang spectrum\n"
"at Trotter error nila. Maaaring lumitaw ang pagkakaiba *pagkatapos* lamang ng isang encoding, kung saan ang index ang nagpapasya kung aling mga qubit ang magkatabi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct the time-evolution circuit {#construct-the-time-evolution-circuit}"
msgstr "Buuin ang time-evolution circuit {#construct-the-time-evolution-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the Hamiltonian to construct its time evolution as a **fermionic circuit**.\n"
"A `FermionicCircuit` has one wire per fermionic mode, not per qubit, and a single `Evolution` gate holds the whole Hamiltonian.\n"
"The following code builds the circuit for $L = 2$ (four modes, which is small enough to read), before any encoding or qubits are involved.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gamitin ang Hamiltonian para buuin ang time evolution nito bilang isang **fermionic circuit**.\n"
"Ang `FermionicCircuit` ay may isang wire bawat fermionic mode, hindi bawat qubit, at ang isang `Evolution` gate ay naglalaman ng buong Hamiltonian.\n"
"Binubuo ng sumusunod na code ang circuit para sa $L = 2$ (apat na mode, na sapat na maliit para mabasa), bago masangkot ang anumang encoding o qubit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c81043f3-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/c81043f3-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `FermionicLieTrotter` synthesis splits that gate by the groups that `flow_set_groups` sets, into one `Evolution` gate per flow\n"
"set. A single call to `decompose()` shows the split. At this small size, the two orderings look alike, because every term acts on two\n"
"modes, and the only difference is *which* two modes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hinahati ng synthesis na `FermionicLieTrotter` ang gate na iyon ayon sa mga group na itinakda ng `flow_set_groups`, tungo sa isang `Evolution` gate bawat flow\n"
"set. Ipinapakita ng isang tawag sa `decompose()` ang paghahati. Sa maliit na size na ito, magkamukha ang dalawang ordering, dahil bawat term ay kumikilos sa dalawa\n"
"na mode, at ang pagkakaiba lang ay *aling* dalawang mode.\n"

