# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Validate the time-evolution circuit {#validate-the-time-evolution-circuit}"
msgstr "I-validate ang time-evolution circuit {#validate-the-time-evolution-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before you continue, compare the results with an independent implementation.\n"
"The `fermi_hubbard_1d` function of ffsim uses $-t\\sum(\\dots) + U' \\sum n_\\uparrow n_\\downarrow - \\mu \\sum n$. This Hamiltonian equals the\n"
"Hamiltonian of this tutorial for $U' = U/2$ and $\\mu = U/4$, up to the constant $UL/8$. Therefore, the lowest eigenvalue at half filling must be the same.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bago magpatuloy, ihambing ang mga resulta sa isang independiyenteng implementasyon.\n"
"Ang function na `fermi_hubbard_1d` ng ffsim ay gumagamit ng $-t\\sum(\\dots) + U' \\sum n_\\uparrow n_\\downarrow - \\mu \\sum n$. Ang Hamiltonian na ito ay katumbas ng\n"
"Hamiltonian ng tutorial na ito para sa $U' = U/2$ at $\\mu = U/4$, hanggang sa constant na $UL/8$. Kaya, dapat pareho ang pinakamababang eigenvalue sa half filling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The same cell also checks the circuit itself. `FermionicCircuit` implements the `apply_unitary` protocol of ffsim, so ffsim can apply the\n"
"time-evolution circuit to a state vector directly. The code compares the result with the matrix exponential of the Hamiltonian, applied to\n"
"the same random state in the half-filling sector.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sinusuri rin ng parehong cell ang mismong circuit. Ipinapatupad ng `FermionicCircuit` ang `apply_unitary` protocol ng ffsim, kaya direktang maiaaplay ng ffsim ang\n"
"time-evolution circuit sa isang state vector. Inihahambing ng code ang resulta sa matrix exponential ng Hamiltonian, na inilapat sa\n"
"parehong random na state sa half-filling sector.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Encoding the fermions in qubits {#3-encoding-the-fermions-in-qubits}"
msgstr "3. Pag-encode ng mga fermion sa mga qubit {#3-encoding-the-fermions-in-qubits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The choice of spin ordering starts to matter when an encoding maps the modes to qubits, because the mode index then decides which qubits are neighbors.\n"
"To see this effect, use the same one-ancilla flow-set encoding that section 1 uses for the spinless case.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagiging mahalaga ang pagpili ng spin ordering kapag minamapa ng isang encoding ang mga mode sa mga qubit, dahil ang mode index na ang magpapasya kung aling mga qubit ang magkatabi.\n"
"Para makita ang epektong ito, gamitin ang parehong one-ancilla flow-set encoding na ginagamit ng section 1 para sa spinless na kaso.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The effect appears as a Pauli pattern, which is a Pauli string together with the offsets of the qubits that it acts on. For example, `ZZ @ (0, 2)` is a Z on some qubit\n"
"$q$ and a Z on qubit $q+2$. The following table prints the patterns for each flow set. The patterns describe only the encoding register, not a\n"
"QPU. The layout decides how far apart two qubits are on a device.\n"
msgstr ""
"Lumilitaw ang epekto bilang Pauli pattern, na isang Pauli string kasama ang mga offset ng mga qubit na kinikilusan nito. Halimbawa, ang `ZZ @ (0, 2)` ay isang Z sa isang qubit\n"
"$q$ at isang Z sa qubit na $q+2$. Piniprint ng sumusunod na table ang mga pattern para sa bawat flow set. Inilalarawan lamang ng mga pattern ang encoding register, hindi isang\n"
"QPU. Ang layout ang nagpapasya kung gaano kalayo ang dalawang qubit sa isang device.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The east (`0`) and west (`1`) flow sets of the *blocked* ordering are the same as in the spinless case, because the hopping terms still act on nearest neighbors.\n"
"The on-site interaction terms, however, become weight-4 and scale with the length $L$ of the chain, as the pattern `ZZZZ @ (0, 1, L, L + 1)` shows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang east (`0`) at west (`1`) na flow set ng *blocked* ordering ay pareho sa spinless na kaso, dahil ang mga hopping term ay kumikilos pa rin sa mga pinakamalapit na kapitbahay.\n"
"Gayunpaman, ang mga on-site interaction term ay nagiging weight-4 at lumalaki kasabay ng haba $L$ ng chain, gaya ng ipinapakita ng pattern na `ZZZZ @ (0, 1, L, L + 1)`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In contrast, in the interleaved ordering, none of the encoded flow sets scale with the size of the system.\n"
"The on-site interaction terms remain weight-2 and are identical to the spinless case, because they act on nearest neighbors. The cost is more expensive hopping terms (`YY` and `ZXXZ`).\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kabilang banda, sa interleaved ordering, wala sa mga na-encode na flow set ang lumalaki kasabay ng size ng sistema.\n"
"Ang mga on-site interaction term ay nananatiling weight-2 at kapareho ng sa spinless na kaso, dahil kumikilos sila sa mga pinakamalapit na kapitbahay. Ang kapalit ay mas mamahaling hopping term (`YY` at `ZXXZ`).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Pauli strings alone do not decide which ordering is cheaper in practice. The answer depends on\n"
"**which qubits the hardware can place next to each other**, and that connectivity is not necessarily one-dimensional.\n"
"A QPU can place the two chains of blocked order side by side, which a single line cannot do. Section 5 uses this property.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi lang ang mga Pauli string ang nagpapasya kung aling ordering ang mas mura sa praktika. Ang sagot ay depende sa\n"
"**kung aling mga qubit ang kayang ilagay ng hardware nang magkatabi**, at ang connectivity na iyon ay hindi kinakailangang isang-dimensyon.\n"
"Maaaring ilagay ng isang QPU ang dalawang chain ng blocked order nang magkatabi, na hindi kayang gawin ng iisang linya. Ginagamit ng Section 5 ang katangiang ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile the `FermionicCircuit` {#transpile-the-fermioniccircuit}"
msgstr "I-transpile ang `FermionicCircuit` {#transpile-the-fermioniccircuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As shown previously, a single Trotter step is one `Evolution` gate that `FermionicLieTrotter` splits into one gate per flow set.\n"
"The `product_formula` argument of `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` then decides how each flow set becomes qubit gates.\n"
"This tutorial compares two synthesis paths:\n"
msgstr ""
"Gaya ng ipinakita kanina, ang isang Trotter step ay isang `Evolution` gate na hinahati ng `FermionicLieTrotter` tungo sa isang gate bawat flow set.\n"
"Ang argument na `product_formula` ng `MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis` ang magpapasya kung paano magiging qubit gates ang bawat flow set.\n"
"Ihahambing ng tutorial na ito ang dalawang synthesis path:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Qiskit `LieTrotter` synthesis, which synthesizes every Pauli rotation separately, in the order that it receives them.\n"
msgstr "Ang Qiskit `LieTrotter` synthesis, na nagsi-synthesize ng bawat Pauli rotation nang hiwalay, sa pagkakasunod-sunod na natatanggap nito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A custom `FlowSetSynthesis` class (defined in the following cell) that uses the structure of the flow sets. It recognizes every Pauli shape that the\n"
"encodings in this tutorial produce (`X`, `ZXZ`, `YY`, `ZXXZ`, `ZZ`, and, for two chains, the `ZZZZ` plaquettes), and\n"
"diagonalizes each flow set with a single Clifford layer. For these Hamiltonians, it does not need a term-by-term fallback,\n"
"and the code asserts that every term matches a known shape.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isang custom na klaseng `FlowSetSynthesis` (idinefine sa susunod na cell) na gumagamit ng istruktura ng mga flow set. Kinikilala nito ang bawat Pauli shape na\n"
"gagawin ng mga encoding sa tutorial na ito (`X`, `ZXZ`, `YY`, `ZXXZ`, `ZZ`, at, para sa dalawang chain, ang mga `ZZZZ` plaquette), at\n"
"nagdi-diagonalize ng bawat flow set gamit ang isang Clifford layer. Para sa mga Hamiltonian na ito, hindi nito kailangan ng term-by-term na fallback,\n"
"at iginigiit ng code na tumutugma ang bawat term sa kilalang shape.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Work is in progress on an implementation that can find a low-depth diagonalizing Clifford circuit automatically.\n"
"Future releases of `qiskit-fermions` plan to support this feature, which can greatly simplify the use of flow-set-based fermion-to-qubit encodings.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
"The following helper function constructs the transpiler pipeline and applies it to the `FermionicCircuit`.\n"
"The function is useful in this tutorial because the flow-set encoding requires a `CustomF2QLayout`, which couples the transpiler pipeline to the fermionic circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Isinasagawa ang trabaho sa isang implementasyon na kayang awtomatikong maghanap ng low-depth na diagonalizing Clifford circuit.\n"
"Plano ng mga susunod na release ng `qiskit-fermions` na suportahan ang feature na ito, na maaaring lubos na magpasimple sa paggamit ng mga flow-set-based na fermion-to-qubit encoding.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
"Binubuo ng sumusunod na helper function ang transpiler pipeline at inilalapat ito sa `FermionicCircuit`.\n"
"Nakakatulong ang function sa tutorial na ito dahil nangangailangan ang flow-set encoding ng `CustomF2QLayout`, na nag-uugnay sa transpiler pipeline sa fermionic circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Scaling of the interleaved mode ordering {#4-scaling-of-the-interleaved-mode-ordering}"
msgstr "4. Pag-scale ng interleaved mode ordering {#4-scaling-of-the-interleaved-mode-ordering}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Start with the interleaved ordering and the encoding of section 3. With the one ancilla, there are $2L + 1$ qubits in a row. The\n"
"flow sets are `YY @ (0, 1)`, `ZXXZ @ (0, 1, 2, 3)`, and `ZZ @ (0, 2)`, and `FlowSetSynthesis` has a one-Clifford recipe for\n"
"each one. Build the circuit for $L = 4$ (`L_SMALL`, the size of every explicit check), and compare it with\n"
"`LieTrotter` before you measure anything.\n"
msgstr ""
"Magsimula sa interleaved ordering at sa encoding ng section 3. Sa isang ancilla, may $2L + 1$ qubit sa isang hilera. Ang\n"
"mga flow set ay `YY @ (0, 1)`, `ZXXZ @ (0, 1, 2, 3)`, at `ZZ @ (0, 2)`, at may one-Clifford recipe ang `FlowSetSynthesis` para sa\n"
"bawat isa. Buuin ang circuit para sa $L = 4$ (`L_SMALL`, ang size ng bawat tahasang pagsusuri), at ihambing ito sa\n"
"`LieTrotter` bago ka magsukat ng anuman.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The previous check shows that the two circuits give identical results, up to a global phase.\n"
"The following drawing shows the regular structure that the flow-set encoding produces in the qubit circuit.\n"
"Later sections show how this structure helps you scale to larger systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapakita ng nakaraang pagsusuri na magkapareho ang resulta ng dalawang circuit, hanggang sa isang global phase.\n"
"Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na drawing ang regular na istrukturang nagagawa ng flow-set encoding sa qubit circuit.\n"
"Ipinapakita ng mga susunod na seksyon kung paano nakakatulong ang istrukturang ito sa pag-scale sa mas malalaking sistema.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/67a517b7-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/67a517b7-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why the circuit needs routing {#why-the-circuit-needs-routing}"
msgstr "Bakit kailangan ng routing ang circuit {#why-the-circuit-needs-routing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every gate of this circuit acts on qubits that are neighbors along the encoding chain, except the gates of the `ZZ` flow set.\n"
"That flow set couples qubits that are two apart (`ZZ @ (0, 2)`, as shown in the table in section 3). On hardware that couples only neighbors, such a pair needs a\n"
"SWAP gate, and the router must insert it. The weakest connectivity that you can use is a plain line of $2L + 1$ qubits. The following code\n"
"counts how many two-qubit gates act on a pair that the line does not couple, for both the term-by-term `LieTrotter` circuit and\n"
"the flow-set circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bawat gate ng circuit na ito ay kumikilos sa mga qubit na magkatabi sa encoding chain, maliban sa mga gate ng `ZZ` flow set.\n"
"Ang flow set na iyon ay nagko-couple ng mga qubit na dalawang puwesto ang layo (`ZZ @ (0, 2)`, gaya ng ipinapakita sa table sa section 3). Sa hardware na nagko-couple lamang ng magkakatabi, ang ganoong pares ay nangangailangan ng\n"
"SWAP gate, at dapat itong ipasok ng router. Ang pinakamahinang connectivity na magagamit mo ay isang simpleng linya ng $2L + 1$ qubit. Binibilang ng sumusunod na code\n"
"kung ilang two-qubit gate ang kumikilos sa pares na hindi ko-couple ng linya, para sa parehong term-by-term na `LieTrotter` circuit at\n"
"flow-set circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The number of gates that are not on a coupler of the line is the same for both circuits: $2L$ at every size (8 at\n"
"$L = 4$, 100 at $L = 50$). These gates come from the `ZZ @ (0, 2)` pairs. There are $L$ of these pairs, and each one becomes two entangling\n"
"gates. `LieTrotter` already produces a diagonal `ZZ` rotation as a single `rzz` gate, as the flow-set synthesis does, so\n"
"both circuits contain the same $L$ distance-two `rzz` gates. The circuits differ in their total number of gates (884 for\n"
"`LieTrotter` compared with 692 for the flow set at $L = 50$). Therefore, the share of gates that are not on a coupler is 11% compared with 14% at $L = 50$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pareho ang bilang ng mga gate na wala sa coupler ng linya sa parehong circuit: $2L$ sa bawat size (8 sa\n"
"$L = 4$, 100 sa $L = 50$). Ang mga gate na ito ay galing sa mga pares na `ZZ @ (0, 2)`. May $L$ na ganitong pares, at ang bawat isa ay nagiging dalawang entangling\n"
"gate. Ang `LieTrotter` ay gumagawa na ng diagonal na `ZZ` rotation bilang isang `rzz` gate, tulad ng flow-set synthesis, kaya\n"
"parehong may $L$ na distance-two na `rzz` gate ang dalawang circuit. Nagkakaiba ang mga circuit sa kabuuang bilang ng mga gate (884 para sa\n"
"`LieTrotter` kumpara sa 692 para sa flow set sa $L = 50$). Kaya, ang bahagi ng mga gate na wala sa coupler ay 11% kumpara sa 14% sa $L = 50$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The routing problem is the same for both circuits. The synthesis changes the rest of the circuit: the hopping terms (`YY` and\n"
"`ZXXZ`). `LieTrotter` synthesizes these terms one by one, and the flow-set synthesis uses one Clifford circuit for the whole flow set.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pareho ang routing problem para sa parehong circuit. Binabago ng synthesis ang natitirang bahagi ng circuit: ang mga hopping term (`YY` at\n"
"`ZXXZ`). Isa-isang sini-synthesize ng `LieTrotter` ang mga term na ito, at gumagamit ang flow-set synthesis ng isang Clifford circuit para sa buong flow set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Find a chain on a QPU {#find-a-chain-on-a-qpu}"
msgstr "Maghanap ng chain sa isang QPU {#find-a-chain-on-a-qpu}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To route onto a QPU, pick a chain of $2L + 1$ qubits on it. The routing task is then the same as on a line. The chain links are couplers, the `ZZ`\n"
"pairs are two apart along the chain, and the layout decides only which physical qubits the chain uses.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para mag-route sa isang QPU, pumili ng chain na $2L + 1$ qubit dito. Pareho na ang routing task sa nasa isang linya. Ang mga link ng chain ay mga coupler, ang mga `ZZ`\n"
"na pares ay dalawang puwesto ang layo sa chain, at ang layout lang ang nagpapasya kung aling mga physical qubit ang gagamitin ng chain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The tutorial uses fake backends for two QPUs, so the comparison is of structure, not noise:\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang tutorial ng mga fake backend para sa dalawang QPU, kaya istruktura ang inihahambing, hindi noise:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Heron** (`FakeFez`): 156 qubits on a heavy-hex lattice. The lattice has no 4-cycles, but it does contain long simple paths.\n"
msgstr "**Heron** (`FakeFez`): 156 qubits sa heavy-hex lattice. Walang 4-cycle ang lattice, ngunit may mahahabang simpleng path ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Nighthawk** (`FakeNighthawk`): 120 qubits on a square lattice of 12 rows and 10 columns. A snake through the rows is a path.\n"
msgstr "**Nighthawk** (`FakeNighthawk`): 120 qubits sa square lattice na 12 row at 10 column. Ang snake sa mga row ay isang path.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `find_path` function searches for a path of a given length on any coupling map. It uses a depth-first search, and always prefers the qubit with the fewest\n"
"free neighbors. The `nighthawk_snake` function walks the rows of Nighthawk.\n"
msgstr ""
"Naghahanap ang function na `find_path` ng path na may ibinigay na haba sa anumang coupling map. Gumagamit ito ng depth-first search, at laging mas pinipili ang qubit na may pinakakaunting\n"
"libreng kapitbahay. Ang function na `nighthawk_snake` ay lumalakad sa mga row ng Nighthawk.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following drawing shows the chains that the two functions return for $L = 50$ (101 qubits), the largest size in this tutorial. Each QPU is\n"
"drawn in full. The gray lines are its couplers, and the light gray circles are the qubits that the circuit does not use. Each colored\n"
"circle is a virtual qubit of the encoded circuit and shows its number. Dark blue circles are spin up (even numbers), light blue circles are\n"
"spin down (odd numbers), and the green circle is the ancilla (the last qubit, $2L$). The dark lines are the chain links between\n"
"consecutive virtual qubits, and they all lie on couplers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na drawing ang mga chain na ibinabalik ng dalawang function para sa $L = 50$ (101 qubits), ang pinakamalaking size sa tutorial na ito. Ang bawat QPU ay\n"
"buong iginuhit. Ang mga kulay-abong linya ay ang mga coupler nito, at ang mga matingkad na kulay-abong bilog ay ang mga qubit na hindi ginagamit ng circuit. Ang bawat kulay na\n"
"bilog ay isang virtual qubit ng na-encode na circuit at nagpapakita ng numero nito. Ang madilim na asul na bilog ay spin up (even na numero), ang matingkad na asul na bilog ay\n"
"spin down (odd na numero), at ang berdeng bilog ay ang ancilla (ang huling qubit, $2L$). Ang mga madilim na linya ay ang mga chain link sa pagitan ng\n"
"magkakasunod na virtual qubit, at lahat ng ito ay nasa mga coupler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On Nighthawk, the chain follows the rows of the square lattice in a snake pattern\n"
"and fills ten of its twelve rows. A shorter chain is the beginning of the same snake. On Heron, the chain winds through the\n"
"heavy-hex lattice, and the search finds a different path for every length.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa Nighthawk, sinusundan ng chain ang mga row ng square lattice sa snake pattern\n"
"at pinupuno ang sampu sa labindalawang row nito. Ang mas maikling chain ay ang simula ng parehong snake. Sa Heron, umiikot ang chain sa\n"
"heavy-hex lattice, at nakakahanap ang paghahanap ng ibang path para sa bawat haba.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The longest 1D chain that you can find on a Heron QPU is 127 qubits long, which allows 63 spinful sites in this case study.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Ang pinakamahabang 1D chain na mahahanap mo sa isang Heron QPU ay 127 qubits ang haba, na nagpapahintulot ng 63 spinful na site sa case study na ito.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When you transpile for real hardware, take the actual noise and calibration data into account to find the\n"
"best layout on the QPU.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nag-transpile ka para sa totoong hardware, isaalang-alang ang aktwal na noise at calibration data para mahanap ang\n"
"pinakamahusay na layout sa QPU.\n"

