msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/0c8d3dd9-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Routing and the role of the seeds {#routing-and-the-role-of-the-seeds}"
msgstr "Routing at ang papel ng mga seed {#routing-and-the-role-of-the-seeds}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The metrics for routing are the **two-qubit depth** and the **two-qubit gate count** after the preset pass manager at\n"
"optimization level 3, in a given basis. The default basis in this tutorial is `{cz, rz, sx, x}`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga sukatan para sa routing ay ang **two-qubit depth** at ang **bilang ng two-qubit gate** pagkatapos ng preset pass manager sa\n"
"optimization level 3, sa isang ibinigay na basis. Ang default na basis sa tutorial na ito ay `{cz, rz, sx, x}`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Which part is random?* The layout is fixed, but the router is not deterministic across seeds. The Qiskit `SabreSwap` pass runs\n"
"several randomized trials (20 at optimization level 3), seeded from the `seed_transpiler` value that you pass, and keeps the trial with\n"
"the fewest SWAP gates. Therefore, a seed fixes the whole set of trials, and a different seed gives a different set. The router has\n"
"work to do on every layout, because of the `ZZ` pairs that the previous section counted. Different seeds find different SWAP gates, and the\n"
"router selects by SWAP count, not by two-qubit depth. For these reasons, the code routes every circuit with 20 seeds and **keeps the best result**: the\n"
"smallest two-qubit depth, with ties going to the smaller gate count. The gate count that this tutorial reports is the count of that same circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Aling bahagi ang random?* Nakapirmi ang layout, ngunit hindi deterministic ang router sa iba't ibang seed. Ang Qiskit `SabreSwap` pass ay nagpapatakbo ng\n"
"maraming randomized na trial (20 sa optimization level 3), na naka-seed mula sa value ng `seed_transpiler` na ipinapasa mo, at pinapanatili ang trial na may\n"
"pinakakaunting SWAP gate. Kaya, ang isang seed ay nagpapirmi sa buong set ng mga trial, at ang ibang seed ay nagbibigay ng ibang set. May\n"
"trabaho ang router sa bawat layout, dahil sa mga `ZZ` na pares na binilang ng nakaraang seksyon. Nakakahanap ang magkakaibang seed ng magkakaibang SWAP gate, at\n"
"pumipili ang router ayon sa bilang ng SWAP, hindi ayon sa two-qubit depth. Dahil dito, nagro-route ang code ng bawat circuit gamit ang 20 seed at **pinapanatili ang pinakamahusay na resulta**: ang\n"
"pinakamaliit na two-qubit depth, at kapag magkapantay, ang mas maliit na bilang ng gate. Ang bilang ng gate na iniuulat ng tutorial na ito ay ang bilang ng parehong circuit na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fractional gates: a second gate set {#fractional-gates-a-second-gate-set}"
msgstr "Mga fractional gate: pangalawang gate set {#fractional-gates-a-second-gate-set}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IBM Heron and Nighthawk devices can run `rzz(theta)` for $0 < \\theta \\le \\pi/2$ and `rx(theta)` for any $\\theta$ as native\n"
"gates. These *fractional gates* are experimental and are off by default. On a real backend, you turn them on with\n"
"`QiskitRuntimeService.backend(\"ibm_torino\", use_fractional_gates=True)`. This setting is a *backend* option, not a transpiler flag.\n"
"The returned `Target` contains `rzz` with `angle_bounds=[(0, pi/2)]`, and `rx`, and the transpiler then uses them.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kayang patakbuhin ng mga IBM Heron at Nighthawk device ang `rzz(theta)` para sa $0 < \\theta \\le \\pi/2$ at ang `rx(theta)` para sa anumang $\\theta$ bilang native\n"
"gates. Ang mga *fractional gate* na ito ay experimental at naka-off bilang default. Sa totoong backend, i-on mo ang mga ito gamit ang\n"
"`QiskitRuntimeService.backend(\"ibm_torino\", use_fractional_gates=True)`. Ang setting na ito ay isang *backend* option, hindi isang transpiler flag.\n"
"Ang ibinabalik na `Target` ay naglalaman ng `rzz` na may `angle_bounds=[(0, pi/2)]`, at `rx`, at ginagamit na ito ng transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code routes every circuit on the QPUs twice: onto the plain `{cz, rz, sx, x}` default basis, and\n"
"onto a fractional target. A two-qubit layer is a layer of `cz` **or** `rzz` gates, and each of these gates counts as one two-qubit gate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalawang beses nire-route ng code ang bawat circuit sa mga QPU: sa simpleng default basis na `{cz, rz, sx, x}`, at\n"
"sa isang fractional target. Ang isang two-qubit layer ay layer ng mga `cz` **o** `rzz` gate, at ang bawat isa sa mga gate na ito ay binibilang bilang isang two-qubit gate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`FakeFez` and `FakeNighthawk` in this environment do not include fractional gates, so the next cell **builds the targets manually**,\n"
"based on the assumptions that are documented in the cell. The depths that later cells report therefore show what the transpiler can do with\n"
"such a gate set. They do not show what a real backend with fractional gates delivers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walang fractional gates ang `FakeFez` at `FakeNighthawk` sa environment na ito, kaya ang susunod na cell ay **mano-manong gumagawa ng mga target**,\n"
"batay sa mga assumption na nakadokumento sa cell. Kaya ang mga depth na iuulat ng mga susunod na cell ay nagpapakita kung ano ang kayang gawin ng transpiler sa\n"
"ganitong gate set. Hindi nito ipinapakita kung ano ang naihahatid ng totoong backend na may fractional gates.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Route onto the QPUs, in both gate sets {#route-onto-the-qpus-in-both-gate-sets}"
msgstr "I-route sa mga QPU, sa parehong gate set {#route-onto-the-qpus-in-both-gate-sets}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code routes the flow-set circuit onto Heron and onto Nighthawk with the chains from the previous section. For comparison, it also routes the `LieTrotter` circuit and the flow-set circuit onto a plain line.\n"
msgstr "Ang sumusunod na code ay nagre-route ng flow-set circuit sa Heron at sa Nighthawk gamit ang mga chain mula sa nakaraang seksyon. Para sa paghahambing, nire-route din nito ang `LieTrotter` circuit at ang flow-set circuit sa isang simpleng line.\n"

