# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Connectivity of Nighthawk devices {#5-connectivity-of-nighthawk-devices}"
msgstr "5. Connectivity ng mga Nighthawk device {#5-connectivity-of-nighthawk-devices}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The interleaved circuit needs only a path. Suppose the QPU offers more connectivity. The qubits of Nighthawk are on a square\n"
"lattice, and a square lattice contains a **ladder**: two parallel chains whose rungs are real couplers. A ladder is the\n"
"interaction graph of the Hubbard model in blocked order. The spin-up chain is on one rail, the spin-down chain is on the other, and the on-site term acts\n"
"across a rung.\n"
msgstr ""
"Path lang ang kailangan ng interleaved circuit. Ipagpalagay na mas maraming connectivity ang alok ng QPU. Ang mga qubit ng Nighthawk ay nasa square\n"
"lattice, at ang square lattice ay may **ladder**: dalawang parallel na chain na ang mga rung ay totoong coupler. Ang ladder ay ang\n"
"interaction graph ng Hubbard model sa blocked order. Ang spin-up chain ay nasa isang rail, ang spin-down chain ay nasa kabilang rail, at ang on-site term ay kumikilos\n"
"sa kabila ng isang rung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The single-chain encoding of section 4 cannot use the ladder. It places all $2L$ modes along **one** chain. With blocked order,\n"
"the spin-up and spin-down blocks are joined end to end, and the on-site plaquettes stretch across the join. Instead, give\n"
"**each spin its own chain and its own ancilla**:\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi magagamit ng single-chain encoding ng seksyon 4 ang ladder. Inilalagay nito ang lahat ng $2L$ mode sa **iisang** chain. Sa blocked order,\n"
"magkadugtong ang dulo-sa-dulo ng mga spin-up at spin-down block, at ang mga on-site plaquette ay umaabot sa kabila ng dugtungan. Sa halip, bigyan\n"
"**ang bawat spin ng sarili nitong chain at sarili nitong ancilla**:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spin-up modes $0..L-1$ are on qubits $0..L-1$, with the ancilla on qubit $L$.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga spin-up mode na $0..L-1$ ay nasa mga qubit na $0..L-1$, at ang ancilla ay nasa qubit na $L$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spin-down modes $L..2L-1$ are on qubits $L+1..2L$, with the ancilla on qubit $2L+1$.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga spin-down mode na $L..2L-1$ ay nasa mga qubit na $L+1..2L$, at ang ancilla ay nasa qubit na $2L+1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each block uses the same images as before: $V_j = Z_qZ_{q+1}$, $T_{j,j+1} = -X_{q+1}/2$, and $T_{j+1,j} = \\tfrac12 Z_qX_{q+1}Z_{q+2}$,\n"
"where $q$ is the qubit of mode $j$. The total is $2L + 2$ qubits, which is one more than before.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gumagamit ang bawat block ng parehong mga image tulad ng dati: $V_j = Z_qZ_{q+1}$, $T_{j,j+1} = -X_{q+1}/2$, at $T_{j+1,j} = \\tfrac12 Z_qX_{q+1}Z_{q+2}$,\n"
"kung saan ang $q$ ay ang qubit ng mode $j$. Ang kabuuan ay $2L + 2$ qubit, na isa pa kaysa dati.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every flow set is now local on the ladder. The `X` and `ZXZ` terms act along a rail, and the interaction `ZZZZ @ (0, 1, L+1, L+2)` is a 2x2\n"
"plaquette (two neighbors on one rail and the two qubits next to them on the other rail).\n"
msgstr ""
"Lokal na ngayon ang bawat flow set sa ladder. Ang mga term na `X` at `ZXZ` ay kumikilos sa isang rail, at ang interaction na `ZZZZ @ (0, 1, L+1, L+2)` ay isang 2x2\n"
"plaquette (dalawang kapitbahay sa isang rail at ang dalawang qubit sa tabi nila sa kabilang rail).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the encoded space, spin-up and spin-down operators now *commute* instead of anticommuting. This difference has no effect on this\n"
"Hamiltonian, because it contains only bilinears of the same spin and products of vertex operators. An operator with hopping between spins\n"
"raises an error in the action, so it cannot silently give a wrong answer. Perform the same check against\n"
"the known `LieTrotter` circuit as for the single-ancilla interleaved ordering:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa na-encode na space, ang mga spin-up at spin-down operator ay *nagko-commute* na ngayon sa halip na nag-aanticommute. Walang epekto ang pagkakaibang ito sa\n"
"Hamiltonian na ito, dahil naglalaman lang ito ng mga bilinear ng parehong spin at mga product ng vertex operator. Ang operator na may hopping sa pagitan ng mga spin\n"
"ay nagtataas ng error sa action, kaya hindi ito tahimik na makapagbibigay ng maling sagot. Gawin ang parehong check laban sa\n"
"kilalang `LieTrotter` circuit tulad ng sa single-ancilla interleaved ordering:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "A ladder on the QPU {#a-ladder-on-the-qpu}"
msgstr "Isang ladder sa QPU {#a-ladder-on-the-qpu}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A chain of $L + 1$ qubits fits on Nighthawk in a straight line if it has at most 12 qubits (along the 12 rows) or at most 10\n"
"(along the 10 columns). Therefore, up to $L = 11$, the two chains are side by side on two neighboring grid lines, rung by rung, and\n"
"every coupler that the circuit needs is a real coupler. The `folded_ladder` function returns this layout. For larger $L$, it also folds the ladder,\n"
"as section 6 describes. The function also selects the orientation that needs fewer strips, and selects the horizontal orientation if both need the same number.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kasya sa Nighthawk nang tuwid na linya ang chain na may $L + 1$ qubit kung hindi ito lalampas sa 12 qubit (sa kahabaan ng 12 row) o hindi lalampas sa 10\n"
"(sa kahabaan ng 10 column). Kaya, hanggang $L = 11$, magkatabi ang dalawang chain sa dalawang magkalapit na grid line, rung por rung, at\n"
"ang bawat coupler na kailangan ng circuit ay totoong coupler. Ibinabalik ng function na `folded_ladder` ang layout na ito. Para sa mas malaking $L$, tinutupi rin nito ang ladder,\n"
"gaya ng inilalarawan ng seksyon 6. Pinipili rin ng function ang orientation na nangangailangan ng mas kaunting strip, at pinipili ang horizontal na orientation kung pareho ang kailangang bilang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following drawings show both straight cases. For $L = 8$, a chain of 9 qubits fits along the 10 columns, so the ladder is\n"
"horizontal. For $L = 10$, a chain of 11 qubits does not fit along the 10 columns (it needs two strips), but it fits along\n"
"the 12 rows, so the layout uses a vertical ladder.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapakita ng mga sumusunod na drawing ang dalawang tuwid na kaso. Para sa $L = 8$, kasya ang chain na may 9 na qubit sa kahabaan ng 10 column, kaya\n"
"horizontal ang ladder. Para sa $L = 10$, hindi kasya ang chain na may 11 qubit sa kahabaan ng 10 column (nangangailangan ito ng dalawang strip), pero kasya ito sa kahabaan ng\n"
"12 row, kaya gumagamit ang layout ng vertical na ladder.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
