msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/spinful-fermi-hubbard-dynamics/extracted-outputs/9756fef7-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Between $L = 10$ and $L = 12$, the depth of the blocked circuit increases from 10 to 25 in the `cz` basis (from eight to 23 with fractional\n"
"gates), and then stays the same up to $L = 50$. **The fold increases the depth once, not once per strip.** The drawing for $L = 50$ has four\n"
"folds and eight stretched links, and the depth is the same as at $L = 12$, which has one fold. The depth stays the same because the\n"
"depth penalties of all folds occur in parallel.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pagitan ng $L = 10$ at $L = 12$, tumataas ang depth ng blocked circuit mula 10 hanggang 25 sa `cz` basis (mula walo hanggang 23 na may fractional\n"
"gates), at pagkatapos ay nananatiling pareho hanggang $L = 50$. **Isang beses lang tumataas ang depth dahil sa tupi, hindi isang beses bawat strip.** Ang drawing para sa $L = 50$ ay may apat na\n"
"tupi at walong nainat na link, at kapareho ng depth ang sa $L = 12$, na may isang tupi. Nananatiling pareho ang depth dahil ang\n"
"mga depth penalty ng lahat ng tupi ay nangyayari nang magkakasabay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Result of the comparison.** Beyond the width of the QPU, blocked order loses its depth advantage. At $L = 50$, both orderings\n"
"reach 25 in the `cz` basis. The best interleaved seed reaches 22 between $L = 12$ and $L = 40$, but its median is 23 to 25.\n"
"With fractional gates, blocked order (23) is deeper than interleaved order (19). Blocked order still has a lower gate count: 462 compared with 838\n"
"in the `cz` basis (45% fewer) and 412 compared with 592 with fractional gates (30% fewer), at the cost of one more qubit. Fewer gates\n"
"can mean less accumulated error on a real device, which can be a reason to prefer blocked order on a QPU with a ladder. The\n"
"observable that you measure at the end of the circuit can also affect the choice of encoding.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Resulta ng paghahambing.** Lampas sa lapad ng QPU, nawawala ang bentahe sa depth ng blocked order. Sa $L = 50$, parehong ordering ay\n"
"umaabot sa 25 sa `cz` basis. Ang pinakamagandang interleaved seed ay umaabot sa 22 sa pagitan ng $L = 12$ at $L = 40$, pero ang median nito ay 23 hanggang 25.\n"
"Sa fractional gates, mas malalim ang blocked order (23) kaysa sa interleaved order (19). Mas mababa pa rin ang gate count ng blocked order: 462 kumpara sa 838\n"
"sa `cz` basis (45% na mas kaunti) at 412 kumpara sa 592 na may fractional gates (30% na mas kaunti), kapalit ng isa pang qubit. Ang mas kaunting gate\n"
"ay maaaring mangahulugan ng mas kaunting naipong error sa totoong device, na maaaring maging dahilan para piliin ang blocked order sa QPU na may ladder. Ang\n"
"observable na sinusukat mo sa dulo ng circuit ay maaari ring makaapekto sa pagpili ng encoding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**On Heron, which has no ladder, blocked order is much worse.** Its best depth grows from 29 at $L = 4$ to 95 at $L = 50$\n"
"in the `cz` basis (92 with fractional gates), and the median and worst seeds at $L = 50$ give 134 and 166.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Sa Heron, na walang ladder, mas masama nang husto ang blocked order.** Ang pinakamagandang depth nito ay lumalaki mula 29 sa $L = 4$ hanggang 95 sa $L = 50$\n"
"sa `cz` basis (92 na may fractional gates), at ang median at pinakamasamang seed sa $L = 50$ ay nagbibigay ng 134 at 166.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Beyond one dimension {#7-beyond-one-dimension}"
msgstr "7. Lampas sa isang dimensyon {#7-beyond-one-dimension}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"All of the previous sections are one-dimensional, where the hardware needs to hold only a path or a ladder. A square lattice of sites is\n"
"the case where the square connectivity of Nighthawk matters most, so this section briefly examines it. To keep the section short, it omits spin\n"
"and uses the **spinless** model of the [Simulate 2D Fermi-Hubbard dynamics with flow sets](/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/2-d-fermi-hubbard) guide\n"
"(Gandon et al., arXiv:2512.11418). That model has hopping and interaction on every nearest-neighbor bond of an $R \\times C$ lattice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang lahat ng nakaraang seksyon ay one-dimensional, kung saan path o ladder lang ang kailangang hawakan ng hardware. Ang square lattice ng mga site ay\n"
"ang kasong pinakamahalaga ang square connectivity ng Nighthawk, kaya sandali itong sinusuri ng seksyong ito. Para paikliin ang seksyon, inaalis nito ang spin\n"
"at ginagamit ang **spinless** na model ng gabay na [Simulate 2D Fermi-Hubbard dynamics with flow sets](/addons/qiskit-fermions/guides/2-d-fermi-hubbard)\n"
"(Gandon et al., arXiv:2512.11418). Ang model na iyon ay may hopping at interaction sa bawat nearest-neighbor bond ng $R \\times C$ lattice.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the Verstraete-Cirac encoding of the model, every site gets **its own ancilla** ($N = RC$ modes use $2N$ qubits), and the hopping splits into **four flow\n"
"sets** (east, west, north, and south). A Clifford circuit of two-qubit depth 2, which acts on all rows or all columns\n"
"at the same time, diagonalizes each flow set. As in 1D, the depth of the circuit therefore does not grow with the lattice. The guide shows each of these steps, but it\n"
"does not transpile to a given connectivity. The following drawing shows how the model fits on Nighthawk.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa Verstraete-Cirac encoding ng model, bawat site ay may **sarili nitong ancilla** ($N = RC$ mode ay gumagamit ng $2N$ qubit), at ang hopping ay nahahati sa **apat na flow\n"
"set** (silangan, kanluran, hilaga, at timog). Ang Clifford circuit na may two-qubit depth na 2, na kumikilos sa lahat ng row o lahat ng column\n"
"sabay-sabay, ay nagdi-diagonalize sa bawat flow set. Tulad sa 1D, ang depth ng circuit ay hindi lumalaki kasabay ng lattice. Ipinapakita ng gabay ang bawat isa sa mga hakbang na ito, pero\n"
"hindi ito nagta-transpile sa isang ibinigay na connectivity. Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na drawing kung paano kasya ang model sa Nighthawk.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The stripe layout on Nighthawk.** Lattice row $r$ runs down QPU column $r$ as a stripe that alternates site, ancilla, site,\n"
"ancilla (lattice column $c$ is on QPU rows $2c$ and $2c+1$). A site and its own ancilla are neighbors, an ancilla and the *next*\n"
"site along the row are neighbors, and vertical neighbors are on adjacent QPU columns. Therefore, **all hopping terms are on couplers**, and\n"
"the Clifford circuits need no routing. The interaction between two sites of the same row is not native, because the two sites are two QPU qubits\n"
"apart, with the ancilla between them (the red arcs). These pairs are the same $\\texttt{ZZ}$-type pairs that you routed in 1D, with one `rzz` gate per\n"
"horizontal bond, so the routing cost is similar to the cost in 1D. The largest lattice that fits this layout is $10 \\times 6$\n"
"(60 sites, which use all 120 qubits).\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang stripe layout sa Nighthawk.** Ang lattice row $r$ ay tumatakbo pababa sa QPU column $r$ bilang stripe na salitan ang site, ancilla, site,\n"
"ancilla (ang lattice column $c$ ay nasa mga QPU row na $2c$ at $2c+1$). Magkapitbahay ang isang site at ang sarili nitong ancilla, magkapitbahay ang isang ancilla at ang *susunod*\n"
"na site sa kahabaan ng row, at ang mga vertical na kapitbahay ay nasa magkatabing QPU column. Kaya, **ang lahat ng hopping term ay nasa mga coupler**, at\n"
"hindi na kailangan ng routing ng mga Clifford circuit. Hindi native ang interaction sa pagitan ng dalawang site ng parehong row, dahil dalawang QPU qubit\n"
"ang pagitan ng dalawang site, na may ancilla sa gitna (ang mga pulang arko). Ang mga pares na ito ay ang parehong $\\texttt{ZZ}$-type na pares na na-route mo sa 1D, na may isang `rzz` gate bawat\n"
"horizontal na bond, kaya katulad ng gastos sa 1D ang gastos sa routing. Ang pinakamalaking lattice na kasya sa layout na ito ay $10 \\times 6$\n"
"(60 site, na gumagamit ng lahat ng 120 qubit).\n"

