# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "8. Takeaways and next steps {#8-takeaways-and-next-steps}"
msgstr "8. Mga takeaway at susunod na hakbang {#8-takeaways-and-next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code summarizes the circuit cost of a single Trotter step with the flow-set synthesis, for each QPU connectivity.\n"
msgstr "Ibinubuod ng sumusunod na code ang gastos sa circuit ng isang Trotter step gamit ang flow-set synthesis, para sa bawat QPU connectivity.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These results lead to the following high-level takeaways:\n"
msgstr "Ang mga resultang ito ay humahantong sa sumusunod na mga high-level takeaway:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**On Nighthawk, use blocked order with two ancillas.** While the ladder fits on the QPU, its depth is half the depth of\n"
"interleaved order (10 compared with 22 in the `cz` basis at $L = 10$). After the fold, its depth stays at 25 (23 with fractional gates).\n"
"Interleaved order has an equally constant depth in the `cz` basis and a lower depth with fractional gates (25 and 19 at $L = 50$). Therefore, at large sizes,\n"
"interleaved order has a small advantage in depth. The blocked circuit still needs far fewer two-qubit gates: 462\n"
"compared with 838 in the `cz` basis (about 45% fewer), and 412 compared with 592 with fractional gates (about 30% fewer), at the cost of\n"
"one more qubit. Fewer gates can mean less accumulated error on a real device, which can be a reason to prefer blocked order.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Sa Nighthawk, gumamit ng blocked order na may dalawang ancilla.** Habang kasya ang ladder sa QPU, ang depth nito ay kalahati ng depth ng\n"
"interleaved order (10 kumpara sa 22 sa `cz` basis sa $L = 10$). Pagkatapos ng tupi, nananatili ang depth nito sa 25 (23 na may fractional gates).\n"
"Ang interleaved order ay may kasing-pare-parehong depth sa `cz` basis at mas mababang depth na may fractional gates (25 at 19 sa $L = 50$). Kaya, sa malalaking laki,\n"
"may maliit na bentahe sa depth ang interleaved order. Mas kaunting two-qubit gate pa rin ang kailangan ng blocked circuit: 462\n"
"kumpara sa 838 sa `cz` basis (humigit-kumulang 45% na mas kaunti), at 412 kumpara sa 592 na may fractional gates (humigit-kumulang 30% na mas kaunti), kapalit ng\n"
"isa pang qubit. Ang mas kaunting gate ay maaaring mangahulugan ng mas kaunting naipong error sa totoong device, na maaaring maging dahilan para piliin ang blocked order.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Without square connectivity, use interleaved order.** One ancilla and any path through the device give a constant depth on Heron\n"
"too (25 in the `cz` basis and 19 with fractional gates at $L = 50$). On Heron, the blocked variant has no ladder to use. Its best\n"
"depth grows with $L$ (95 and 92 at $L = 50$, and 166 and 161 for the worst routing seed), and fractional gates barely reduce it.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kung walang square connectivity, gumamit ng interleaved order.** Ang isang ancilla at anumang path sa device ay nagbibigay ng pare-parehong depth sa Heron\n"
"rin (25 sa `cz` basis at 19 na may fractional gates sa $L = 50$). Sa Heron, walang ladder na magagamit ang blocked variant. Ang pinakamagandang\n"
"depth nito ay lumalaki kasabay ng $L$ (95 at 92 sa $L = 50$, at 166 at 161 para sa pinakamasamang routing seed), at halos hindi ito binabawasan ng fractional gates.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Fractional gates lower the constant depth.** Where the depth is constant, it drops from 25 to 19 for both interleaved variants and\n"
"from 25 to 23 for blocked order on Nighthawk. At $L = 10$, the depth of the blocked circuit drops from 10 to 8. The gate counts also drop.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pinababa ng fractional gates ang pare-parehong depth.** Kung saan pare-pareho ang depth, bumababa ito mula 25 hanggang 19 para sa parehong interleaved variant at\n"
"mula 25 hanggang 23 para sa blocked order sa Nighthawk. Sa $L = 10$, bumababa ang depth ng blocked circuit mula 10 hanggang 8. Bumababa rin ang mga gate count.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The ordering is a hardware decision, not a physics decision.** Blocked and interleaved order are the same Hamiltonian with\n"
"renamed modes, as the relabeling check in section 2 shows. The ordering changes which modes are neighbors, and the encoding\n"
"and the coupling map see that change.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang ordering ay desisyon ng hardware, hindi desisyon ng physics.** Ang blocked at interleaved order ay iisang Hamiltonian na may\n"
"binagong pangalan ng mga mode, gaya ng ipinapakita ng relabeling check sa seksyon 2. Binabago ng ordering kung aling mga mode ang magkapitbahay, at nakikita ng encoding\n"
"at ng coupling map ang pagbabagong iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**The structure is useful only with a synthesis that uses it.** With a term-by-term synthesis (`LieTrotter`), the depth on a line grows\n"
"linearly, to 599 at $L = 50$, compared with 23 for the flow-set circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kapaki-pakinabang lang ang structure kung may synthesis na gumagamit nito.** Sa term-by-term synthesis (`LieTrotter`), linear na lumalaki ang depth sa isang line,\n"
"hanggang 599 sa $L = 50$, kumpara sa 23 para sa flow-set circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**All results in this tutorial use custom syntheses.** Both circuits use a one-Clifford recipe for every flow set, so the\n"
"comparison is fair, but a different synthesis might change the numbers. Future releases of\n"
"`qiskit-fermions` might automatically find a short-depth diagonalizing Clifford circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Ang lahat ng resulta sa tutorial na ito ay gumagamit ng custom synthesis.** Parehong circuit ay gumagamit ng one-Clifford recipe para sa bawat flow set, kaya\n"
"patas ang paghahambing, pero maaaring baguhin ng ibang synthesis ang mga numero. Ang mga susunod na release ng\n"
"`qiskit-fermions` ay maaaring awtomatikong makahanap ng diagonalizing Clifford circuit na maikli ang depth.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Caveats.** The depths are for noise-free coupling maps (`FakeFez` and `FakeNighthawk`), manually built fractional targets, and\n"
"manually chosen layouts. The best of 20 routing seeds is an optimistic result by design. It is the depth that you can reach if you\n"
"route a circuit many times and keep the best result, which is inexpensive to do before a run. The median is the result of a single transpilation,\n"
"and it is never smaller than the best result. This tutorial compares structure, not fidelity. On Heron, the two-ancilla blocked variant is routed without a manual layout,\n"
"because the heavy-hex lattice has no ladder. A better placement might do somewhat better than the router, but\n"
"the lattice still has no ladder.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Mga babala.** Ang mga depth ay para sa mga noise-free coupling map (`FakeFez` at `FakeNighthawk`), mano-manong ginawang fractional target, at\n"
"mano-manong piniling layout. Ang pinakamagaling sa 20 routing seed ay optimistikong resulta sa disenyo. Ito ang depth na maaabot mo kung\n"
"maraming beses mong ire-route ang circuit at itatago ang pinakamagandang resulta, na mura namang gawin bago ang run. Ang median ay ang resulta ng isang transpilation,\n"
"at hindi ito kailanman mas maliit kaysa sa pinakamagandang resulta. Inihahambing ng tutorial na ito ang structure, hindi ang fidelity. Sa Heron, ang two-ancilla blocked variant ay nire-route nang walang manual na layout,\n"
"dahil walang ladder ang heavy-hex lattice. Maaaring mas gumanda nang kaunti ang resulta ng mas mahusay na placement kaysa sa router, pero\n"
"walang ladder pa rin ang lattice.\n"

